{
  "schema": 1,
  "notes": {
    "what": "The engine knowledge that turns the UI pack (client/ui/theme/pack/toy.pack.json, pinned by ui-sync) into the game's Theme (#288). The pack holds complete StyleBox records per type variation; this file names the Godot 4.7.2 theme item each pack field becomes. tools/theme/theme_builder.gd reads both; tools/theme/build_theme.gd writes the themes; tests/unit/tools/theme_builder_test.gd checks this file against the pack and the engine.",
    "regenerate": "tools\\run.cmd ui-sync ui-<version>, then tools\\run.cmd run tools/theme/build_theme.gd --headless. Never edit game_theme*.tres by hand.",
    "sources": "Item names: the 4.7.2 class reference (theme_items of each class, godot --doctool) and the pack's tokens/README.md (Classes, Items, Textures) at its tag.",
    "not_in_default_theme": "Items the 4.7.2 class reference binds but Godot's default theme does not set (so ThemeDB.get_default_theme() does not list them): the keys test accepts them only from this list.",
    "custom": "Items no engine class binds: the Toy components' code reads them (#289) with get_theme_constant or get_theme_color; the keys test requires that none of them shadows an engine item.",
    "legacy": "Today's screens' names as thin variations of Toy ones (the issue's list, but EscTab follows the dark-context ToyMenuItem: the Esc menu still sits on a dark panel, where ToyTab's ink text is unreadable), so the screens restyle with no code change. HudHint (not in the issue's list) follows ToyHudCaption, a step below HudText's ToyTextOnDark, as a hint is below what it explains. LifeBar keeps its own background: Theme.get_stylebox does not follow variations, and life_panel_test sizes the bar from LifeBar's own StyleBox. Its content margins left and right are #287's greybox value (160 x 5/3), the bar's width on the 1920x1080 base.",
    "keep": "Names the issue does not map to a Toy variation (containers' margins and separations, a few labels): their greybox values as #287 scaled them to the 1920x1080 base, until the screens move to Toy variations (#289 and the screen issues). Not a design decision.",
    "font": "Comfortaa ships with #520 (the font file and its licence). file null: the builder sets only font_size; when #520 lands the font it fills file and the builder sets a FontVariation (weight from each label's fontWeight) and line_spacing from the font's metrics.",
    "textures": "The pack's textures (slider knobs, the dropdown arrow, the radio icons) are SVGs under the pack's .gdignore, so Godot cannot load them from there: #520 imports them into an imported folder under the same sha256 lock and then the builder sets them as theme icons. Until then the builder only checks each texture key against the class's icons below.",
    "hints": "The pack's `base` (the toy base Panel under a raised face, per context) and `toggle` (the selected partner) are not theme items: the builder writes them into each theme's metadata `toy_hints` ({bases: {variation: {context: base}}, toggles: {variation: selected}}), which client/ui/toy_hints.gd reads for ToyRaised and ToyToggle (#289).",
    "deprecated": "Variations the pack marks deprecated (ToyChipNew, ToyChipNewText, ToyHowtoCaption) are not written: no screen uses them and they leave the pack at its next major release.",
    "base_types": "Engine classes the theme styles under their own name (#576), so a bare control the screens build (a LineEdit with no theme_type_variation) has a look: `from` copies every item of a live pack variation of that very class (the same StyleBox objects), and constants, font_sizes and colors give literal items. A theme on a node is searched through a control's whole type chain before Godot's default theme, so a row on a class with engine subclasses would also restyle them (a Button row every CheckBox): the builder refuses a row item that would replace the default theme's own item on a subclass. The literal rows are #287's greybox values (Godot's default x 5/3, rounded) for the classes the pack has no look for, so they keep their apparent size at gui/theme/default_theme_scale 1. Not a design decision.",
    "default_font_size": "The theme's default font size, which a control takes when no type in its chain has a font_size (bare Label, Button, CheckBox, ProgressBar): #287's greybox size, Godot's 16 x 5/3. The same in the large-text theme: the pack has no large value for it. Not a design decision."
  },
